From: mptfire <263163432+mptfire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:44:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] bash, mcp: review follow-ups: no hang on backgrounded
 children, no panic on odd env, named denies

Three gaps found in an adversarial review of the series, plus one honest correction to the sandbox wording shipped separately:

The success path joined the drain threads unconditionally, and a backgrounded child (sleep 5 &) inherits the pipe's write end and holds it open past sh's exit: the result waited out the child's whole lifetime. (The pre-fix code hung identically, read_to_string blocking on the same EOF, so this is an old defect surfaced, not a regression.) The drains now get a 400ms grace to reach EOF, and stragglers holding the write end past the grace get the group kill: the command finished, whatever it backgrounded had its turn.

Both env builders walked vars(), which panics on a non-UTF-8 value: a crash path inside every bash spawn and MCP connect. They walk vars_os now and skip entries that are not valid UTF-8 rather than mangling them.

MCP servers were filtered by shape alone, but the config names credentials by env name (api_key_env), and MY_LLM_CRED matches no shape: connect() takes the config's api_key_env names and denies them by name alongside the shapes. TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM is named innocent explicitly: it contains TOKEN and stripping it degraded a working server.
